        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: Who is the artist of the album \"Giant Steps\"?\n\nDocument:\nInternational Publishing Group Paperback : 956 pages ( Writer/broadcaster/jazz historian Shipton offers a musical analysis of âGiant Steps.â ) See the Reading and Research page for this tune for additional references . - Sandra Burlingame Jazz History Notes Woody Herman -- clarinetist , vocalist , saxophonist and bandleader -- kept a vibrant big band together for 51 years , an achievement equaled only by Duke Ellington . Herman filled his ranks with young talent ( many half his age or less ) , keeping his music fresh and up-to-date . The bandâs 1973 album entitled Giant Steps was the first\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document only says that some answer is wrong, write no card for that answer.\n\nThe fields of a card:\n- \"entity\": who or what this answer is about, as specifically as the document identifies it: the full name, plus the details the document gives that tell it apart from others with the same name (what kind of thing it is, profession or role, nationality or place, years, creator, other names), even where the question does not ask about